 "id": "WIN-ID-02 (Windows pids: the cross-session finish never takes an alive-unknown session as ended)",
 "note": "orphans::pass finishes another session's stash only when sessions::ended holds: every per-process record of it reads gone (record_live -> identity::alive). Under Git Bash's perl a record names Claude Code's Windows pid. Seams as WIN-ID-01: (u) a session whose record names a pid only `ps -W` lists (a claude started from PowerShell: alive-unknown, start null) and (k) one whose start time is recorded but whose pid nothing maps now (alive-unknown) stay unfinished; (m) one whose winpid maps to a running MSYS pid with the recorded /proc start stays live; (g) one whose pid neither maps nor is listed is gone and is finished, by SessionStart's pass (hook.pl), by `reconcile --orphans`, and by the Stop and SessionEnd passes (hook.pl); `reconcile --orphans --full` with no `ps -W` listing (the seam names a missing file) or with one whose layout cannot be read (no header, no row that parses) reads every pid that nothing maps as unknown, never gone: (n), whose pid no listing names, then stays unfinished too, and is finished once a readable listing lacks it",
 "now": "2026-10-21T10:00:00+00:00",
 "tz": "UTC",
